WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.400
All right, this is something a little&nbsp;
different, you know, I get so many emails,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:09.120
probably like eight to 10 emails a week from&nbsp;
people who either want to start a podcast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:13.440
YouTube channel or independent media show or&nbsp;
who have started it. But it's not going as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:18.640
well as they want. And they want advice from me.
And it's beyond the scope of the 24 hours that I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:23.920
have in the day to be doing too much of this kind&nbsp;
of individual guidance. But there are a bunch of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:29.200
different people over the years that have come to&nbsp;
me for advice, people I know personally or people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:35.120
that are introduced to me. And they often have&nbsp;
very similar questions and the point of failure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:40.240
for almost everybody is exactly the same. And&nbsp;
I sort of tweeted about this yesterday and a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:46.400
bunch of people wrote back and said, you should&nbsp;
really kind of talk about this being as not were,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:51.440
I believe, in the top one percent of YouTube&nbsp;
at this point. And having done it and having&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:56.080
gotten to the point of hiring staff and having a&nbsp;
successful business model, what is it that causes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.080 --> 00:01:01.440
people to fail? And unfortunately, fortunately or&nbsp;
unfortunately, the good, I have good news and bad&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:06.080
news, and it's all the same. The biggest single&nbsp;
point of failure is essentially not showing up.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:14.320
When I will talk to people who have started shows&nbsp;
or want to, they often will jump to things like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:21.360
how do I negotiate a brand deal? What should&nbsp;
my YouTube thumbnails look like? What kind of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:28.720
equipment do I need for my podcast? When can&nbsp;
I monetize? And so often the cart is being put&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:35.200
before the horse. And what I tell everybody is&nbsp;
all of that stuff will come naturally. You'll&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:41.680
figure that stuff out when the time comes, once&nbsp;
you are actually steadily and consistently and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:47.760
reliably producing the content. This isn't like&nbsp;
the bogus 98 percent is showing up. This is just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:54.640
the reality that people will often focus on things&nbsp;
that aren't the most important. Now, obviously,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.640 --> 00:02:02.080
if your content is terrible, some people just&nbsp;
like, you know, the content is not good, assuming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:08.560
that your content isn't terrible. Where&nbsp;
almost everybody fails is they get discouraged&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:13.440
too early. There are overnight successes&nbsp;
and independent media. Of course there are,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:20.480
but the vast majority are not. And people will&nbsp;
come to me and say, you need to pick a content&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:25.600
schedule and stick to it. Are you doing a weekly&nbsp;
show? Are you doing daily YouTube clips? Are you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:31.440
doing a twice a week show? Or what is the format&nbsp;
and the timeline that you are committing to?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:38.000
And sometimes people will hear that. And and they&nbsp;
will keep it going, you know, I remember, in fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:45.360
years and years ago meeting up with Kyle Kolinsky&nbsp;
when both of our channels were much smaller.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:51.600
And the thing we talked about as we both were&nbsp;
looking to grow at the time that he actually did,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:56.640
and he now has a channel that that is doing&nbsp;
really well, is you've got to commit to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.640 --> 00:03:00.160
schedule of content. That's actually&nbsp;
the key thing. We didn't talk about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:06.720
monetization, brand deals, thumbnails. We talked&nbsp;
maybe about, you know, what microphone do use,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:10.880
but it was all about the content. And&nbsp;
so I'll have conversations with people.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:15.600
And 90 percent of the conversation is about&nbsp;
things that don't really make a difference. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:20.400
then they'll say, yeah, yeah, I'm going to do the&nbsp;
content. Six months go by, I'll come across their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:25.920
YouTube channel and it'll say, Oh, the latest&nbsp;
video is six weeks old. You've done no content&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:30.720
for six weeks. And sometimes we'll have another&nbsp;
interaction and they'll say, yeah, you know, it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:35.360
just wasn't as lucrative as I wanted it to be, is&nbsp;
it? Well, but you're not publishing the content.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:42.640
You have to do that first. The other big mistake&nbsp;
is sometimes just scaling up expenses before it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:50.560
time. I know of shows that are one tenth the size&nbsp;
of our show. We're the host will tell me they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:56.560
already have an executive assistant who responds&nbsp;
to their email and schedules, their interviews.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.560 --> 00:04:03.680
What, what? That doesn't make any sense. And I&nbsp;
from a business standpoint, I've talked before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:08.480
about the push cart method. One of my MBA&nbsp;
professors would talk about the pushcart method.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:14.160
Don't necessarily go to a restaurant with&nbsp;
an expensive lease and tons of employees&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:22.160
try the food with a pushcart, a food cart. And&nbsp;
if it does, well, then you roll that into maybe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:28.160
getting the restaurant. And this is like the most&nbsp;
important thing that I that I tell people. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:33.200
most of them fail to do it. And there are tons&nbsp;
of shows that could define the contents. Good.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:39.840
But people just don't show up. And so, you&nbsp;
know, unfortunately, I at this point am unable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:46.960
to provide individualized advice to all the people&nbsp;
who email me. But if you're not doing the content,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:51.760
don't be surprised that none of the other stuff&nbsp;
is going as well as you want it to go. Hopefully&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:55.200
that's useful to some people. And I think that&nbsp;
that's what we committed to early with the show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.200 --> 00:05:00.240
which was when we were twice a week, we were twice&nbsp;
a week and we were doing the content and we were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:04.960
putting up the clips in the podcast episodes.&nbsp;
When we went to when when that was supported&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:11.840
financially, we then went to four times a week&nbsp;
and we did it. And then when that was supported&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:17.040
financially, we went to the five and people can&nbsp;
count on the content. It's the most important&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:22.240
thing. It's the biggest point of failure and the&nbsp;
real reason why tons of people I mean, it's dozens&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:26.240
and dozens of people over time who have emailed&nbsp;
me saying I want to do what you're doing, but it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.240 --> 00:05:31.600
just not happening. You didn't do the main thing&nbsp;
I said, which is commit to the content schedule.

